<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arabshahid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1511–18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Arabshahids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arabshahids were a Chinggisid dynasty descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiban">Shiban</a> that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>, the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a>, from 1511. Founded by the brothers Ilbars and Balbars, it ruled first from Urgench and from the 17th century from Khiva. Its best-known member was the 17th-century khan and historian Abu al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> Bahadur. The line weakened in the 18th century, when tribal leaders installed puppet khans, until the Qungrat dynasty took the throne in 1804.</p></div>
